<h1>About</h1>

<p>I am an academic librarian with interests in research, biblical languages, philosophy, and film. I studied Koine Greek and Hebrew at the graduate level, writing my thesis on the concept of lupe — grief as a productive, transformative force in Pauline thought.</p>

<p>This site is a place for careful thinking in short form. Not a blog, not an academic portfolio. Something closer to a commonplace book — thoughts worth keeping, written to be read.</p>

<p>Via lupe is the thread running through all of it. The journey grief makes possible.</p>